# Technical Design Document (TDD) — Mannschaftskasse

## 0. Context and Constraints

- **Project type**: 2-day university project (MVP-first)
- **Primary goal**: Easy maintainability, easy deployment, easy extensibility
- **Business scope**: Football team operations + team cash management (fines, payments, attendance, calendar, reporting)
- **Future scope**: Additional modules (e.g. mobile app, advanced analytics), but strictly single-team.

---

## 1. Technology Evaluation and Decision Rationale

### 1.1 Frontend Options

| Option | Advantages | Disadvantages | Complexity | Learning Curve | Scalability | Maintainability |
|---|---|---|---|---|---|---|
| **Angular** | Strong structure, built-in patterns, enterprise-ready | Heavy for MVP, more boilerplate | High | High | High | High (for larger teams) |
| **React** | Huge ecosystem, flexible, fast UI development | Needs framework choices (routing, state, forms) | Medium | Medium | High | Medium-High (with conventions) |
| **Vue** | Very approachable, clean templates, fast onboarding | Smaller enterprise ecosystem than React | Low-Medium | Low | High | High |
| **Blazor** | C# full-stack alignment | Smaller talent pool in many web teams, hosting/runtime trade-offs | Medium-High | Medium | Medium-High | Medium |
| **Other (SvelteKit)** | Excellent DX, very fast UI | Smaller ecosystem for enterprise tooling | Low-Medium | Low | Medium-High | Medium |

**Recommendation (MVP): `Vue 3 + TypeScript + Vite + Pinia + Vue Router`**
- Fastest path for a small team and short timeline
- Simple component model and low setup overhead
- Good maintainability and extension potential

---

### 1.2 Backend Options

| Option | Advantages | Disadvantages | Complexity | Learning Curve | Scalability | Maintainability |
|---|---|---|---|---|---|---|
| **ASP.NET Core** | Strong performance, robust security, great tooling | More setup overhead for rapid MVP if team not C#-centric | Medium | Medium | High | High |
| **Spring Boot** | Mature ecosystem, enterprise-grade | Heavier footprint and boilerplate for short project | High | High | High | High |
| **Node.js (Express)** | Very fast development, JS/TS full-stack reuse | Requires discipline for architecture | Low-Medium | Low | High | Medium |
| **NestJS** | Structured Node framework, DI, modular design, good docs | Slightly more initial setup than plain Express | Medium | Medium | High | High |
| **Django** | Batteries included, admin panel, strong ORM | Python stack split from JS frontend | Medium | Medium | High | High |
| **Other (FastAPI)** | Very fast API development, strong typing | Smaller all-in-one ecosystem than Django | Low-Medium | Low | High | Medium-High |

**Recommendation (MVP + growth): `NestJS + TypeScript`**
- Balanced speed and structure
- Clean module boundaries for maintainability
- Shared language with frontend reduces cognitive load

---

### 1.3 Database Options

| Option | Advantages | Disadvantages | Complexity | Learning Curve | Scalability | Maintainability |
|---|---|---|---|---|---|---|
| **PostgreSQL** | Rich features, strong integrity, JSON support, great for analytics/reporting | Slightly more operations knowledge than SQLite | Medium | Medium | High | High |
| **MySQL** | Widely used, stable | Less feature-rich for advanced querying vs PostgreSQL | Medium | Medium | High | High |
| **SQL Server** | Enterprise tooling and BI integration | Potential licensing/cost considerations | Medium-High | Medium | High | High |
