## 2. System Overview

### Purpose
A web platform for football team organization and team treasury management (attendance, fines, payments, and reporting).

### Core Business Goals
1. Reduce administrative overhead for coaches/admins
2. Increase player accountability for responses and payments
3. Ensure transparent, auditable team finances
4. Provide actionable team statistics

### Major Modules
- Identity & Access
- Team & Player Management
- Calendar & Attendance
- Fine Catalog & Fine Assignment
- Cash Register & Payments
- Notifications
- Statistics & Reporting
- Audit & Compliance

### Architecture
- **Frontend (Vue SPA)**: UI, workflows, dashboards, role-aware navigation
- **Backend (NestJS API)**: business rules, authorization, integrations, reporting aggregation
- **Database (PostgreSQL)**: source of truth, integrity constraints, audit trail

---

## 3. Roles and Permissions

### Administrator
- **Access**: full admin areas
- **Actions**: manage users, roles, teams, fines, payments, settings
- **Restrictions**: cannot bypass audit logging
- **Data visibility**: all team financial and attendance data

### Coach
- **Access**: calendar, attendance, statistics, fine assignment
- **Actions**: create/edit/cancel events, review attendance reasons, assign fines
- **Restrictions**: no system-level user/role configuration
- **Data visibility**: full attendance + relevant financial summaries

### Player
- **Access**: personal dashboard, own fines/payments, calendar participation
- **Actions**: accept/decline events (decline requires reason), pay fines, view history
- **Restrictions**: no management actions; only own personal financial details
- **Data visibility**: own details + team-level aggregated summaries where allowed

### Treasurer (Kassenwart)
- **Access**: treasury and payment settings
- **Actions**: configure payout/payee details, reconcile incoming payments, register manual income/expenses
- **Restrictions**: no role administration
- **Data visibility**: full financial data, limited attendance detail

