## 9. Non-Functional Requirements

### Security
- JWT auth with short-lived access + refresh token rotation
- Password hashing via Argon2/Bcrypt
- RBAC + resource-level authorization
- CSRF mitigation (if cookie auth), CORS allowlist
- Rate limiting on auth and webhook endpoints

### Privacy/GDPR
- Data minimization, purpose limitation, retention policy
- Export/delete request capability for personal data
- Audit access for sensitive changes

### Performance & Scalability
- P95 API response target: < 300ms for common queries
- Pagination and query optimization on list endpoints
- Stateless backend horizontal scaling

### Reliability & Operations
- Structured logging (JSON), correlation IDs
- Health/readiness checks
- Basic monitoring: uptime, error rate, response time
- Backup strategy for PostgreSQL (daily + retention)

### Maintainability & Testability
- Modular backend architecture
- Typed contracts and API validation
- Unit + integration tests for business rules
- E2E smoke tests for critical workflows

